      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The interpretation of this has been a point of contention since the first nametag-hiding shader was uploaded to go invisible.  I know a lot of \"spook\" avatars use this to sneak around, etc. \nThe TOS explicitly bans: \n\"Impersonating a VRChat employee.\"\n\"You may not falsely identify yourself as another individual or group.\"\nSo my understanding up until now has been that you can't change your nameplate to pretend to be someone else, impersonate a mod, or change the UI in a way that deceives people (ie: Giving yourself a \"Trusted User\" border when you're not, adding a \"Friend\" icon to your nametag, changing your performance ranking icon, etc.) \nIt would be great to have the TOS reflect what is actually banned since the current wording is very vague.\nFor example, \"affect/modify the appearance of the VRChat UI\" would apply to full-screen shaders, distortion effects on water shaders, post-processing in worlds, or even a stray particle flying in front of/behind the nameplate.\nSomething like a guideline on what would consider acceptable vs unacceptable would be nice.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
